==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
-

==='''Chapter 2'''===
This stage is very easy with Awakened Bahamut Cat's [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talent]]. Combine him with units like Fishman Cat, [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] to stop Cat God from getting his third attack in and nuking all your units. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is especially useful here as most enemies are Behemoths, and their damage is great even against non-Behemoths.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage is drastically different from the others, and way more difficult as well. Cat God is buffed to 200% his original stats this time around, and is supported by a dangerous mix of peons.

You can think of this stage as having two phases, the first phases to get you accustomed to Cat God with a cat limit of 15, where barely anything spawns. Use this phase to chip down Cat God and maintain distance. When Deathshund spawns, enemy spawn rates will also spike, starting the second phase. Your survival of this phase will be determined on how successful you were on maintaining ground in the first, as Cat God will shut down all attempts to push by warping your units backwards, and Deathshund will kill anything that didn't get warped.

Don't be perturbed by this, and deal with Deathshund how you normally would by this point, i.e. [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blasting]] him out of the ground, then timing [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCats]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cats]] in between his attack cycles to quickly wear down his HP while stalling with Shigong Cat—who benefits immensely from his [[Immune to Warp]] Talent.

Bring units that can counter the peons, as well as withstand Cat God's Warp Waves (Such as Talented Can Can Cat, [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]] and [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]) and pay attention to the amount of units you send out. While the stage isn't too difficult, coming unprepared can and likely will lead to your defeat.

